  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Key trade-offs",
      "items": [
        "Driver app: Adaptive interval (every ~4s, more often when near a request): every second would be too much load.",
        "Location Svc: “Hot” positions live in memory, not in the on-disk DB.",
        "Geo index: geohash/Redis (great) vs PostGIS quadtree (good) vs B-tree scan (bad, impractical).",
        "Matching Svc: Under contention, a distributed lock with TTL on Redis: don't assign the same driver to two rides."
      ]
    }
